{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head d2ee413bdbcd2f5cd1be2cc2b2b5f56d467f2f58 (tree a684ff486bb0a0d1c921305511df9c324490c8db), the amended OB-L notes on published E5 b77be3f9. The verdict binds the OB-L implementation promise 544617ee and signs both path artifacts, with the implementation note first. It answers the amended request fd746ca4 and replaces my unfiled review of 0e406156, which the planner's ruling 9647a0f4 overtook.\n\n## What changed since 0e406156\nOne commit, \"Set the first Grow route p95 bound\", edits the two notes and nothing else (`git diff 0e406156 d2ee413b`). It applies ruling 9647a0f4 as written:\n- The note keeps 864 ms as the observed Grow route p95 over one 15-minute window with 149 weighted routes. It no longer calls 864 ms the bound.\n- The note sets the first bound at 1,800 ms, \"about twice the observation\" (2 x 864 is 1,728). The bound applies to Grow only.\n- Demo stays uncalibrated, because its window returned no data.\n- The note defers tightening until three more deploy windows exist.\n- Coverage stays `unknown` (sampled window) and deployment acceptance stays open. The design note's Status says both.\nThe ruling asked for one label sentence. The note spreads its content over two adjacent sentences (864 ms, one 15-minute Grow window, 149 weighted routes, about twice), which says the same.\n\n## Evidence\n- **Artifacts.** The two filed artifacts equal the two changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only b77be3f9 d2ee413b`).\n- **Observations.** The evidence tables, hashes and measured values are unchanged from 0e406156, where I verified them against the two evidence directories: the Grow files match their five SHA-256 values and read 149 weighted routes, 71 turns, zero errors, p95 864 ms, coverage `unknown`. The Demo record reads no data.\n- **Ruling reference.** The note names ruling 9647a0f4a68b61b10a0466dbd9df15307236fb14, the full id of the planner's act.\n- **Gate.** The notes-only gate at 13adb42e (tree f788cbb3), `gate.txt` SHA-256 `469f5edc…`, passed, and END act 6f261691 records it. The note now says the continuation added the gate evidence and the ruling updated the two notes, and that source and tests match the gated tree. That is true: no path outside the two notes differs. The ruling skips the gate for a notes-only head.\n- **Checks.** The merge into origin/main (b77be3f9) is clean with tree a684ff48. `git diff --check` is clean. `check-commit-messages` flags none of 3. `check-notes` reports 0 warnings. The added lines carry no other project's name, no `/Users/` path and no private config path.\n\n## Wake rate\nTwo notes change. No alarm, retry or reschedule is added, so the wake floor and requests per room per hour are unchanged.\n\n## Architecture\nThe note keeps the observation (864 ms), the bound (1,800 ms) and the limits (Grow only, coverage unknown, three more windows) apart. It does not claim a calibrated pass.\n\n## Security\nNotes only. Nothing touches a token path, a header or a custody path.\n\n## Simplification\nNothing to remove.\n\n## Non-blocking\n1. **Grow source head.** The Grow section still does not name the source it ran from. `invocation.json` reads 42d35b88, the published E2 head the Demo section names. Add one sentence at the next edit.\n2. **Bound scope.** The 1,800 ms bound is a note-level value. No file in the repository carries it yet, and the deploy-check CLI still needs a calibration record to use it. A later head that records it needs its own review.\n3. **Scratch scripts.** The adapters and launchers live only in the two evidence directories, as in my earlier review.\n\nNo gate is required: the head changes only notes.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2a084b282b11e84e65d76e56a3f050ba26f8fea7","binding":"assigned","head":"d2ee413bdbcd2f5cd1be2cc2b2b5f56d467f2f58","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ace0e69276d80e47261e9566edf1875ed8e7f56